# Build output
/target/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- model weights
#
# Converted checkpoints, several GB each. `scripts/bootstrap.sh` regenerates them from
# the upstream models; see docs/setup.md. Never commit these — the licences belong to
# the upstream model authors, not to this repo.
/references/*/weights/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- fixtures
#
# Reference activations dumped from PyTorch, regenerated by `dump_fixtures.py`. The
# `.json` inventories beside them are small and *are* tracked: they record the tensor
# names and shapes each gate expects, which is worth having in history even when the
# tensors themselves are not.
# Deny everything under a fixture directory, then allow back the small `.json`
# inventories. Listing extensions instead (`*.safetensors`) leaves the hole that a new
# file type — a `.npy`, a `.bin`, a stray `.wav` — is committable by default. That is the
# mechanism by which the book repo ended up with compiled Rust binaries in its history.
/fixtures/*/*
!/fixtures/*/
!/fixtures/*/*.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- audio
#
# Renders are regenerated by `scripts/render-examples.sh`. The two short reference
# clips under examples/ are tracked deliberately (see examples/README.md); everything
# else is scratch.
/examples/diag/
*.wav
!/examples/cosy_short.wav

# Narration output: converted text, rendered audio, and the per-run server logs
# `scripts/narrate.sh` leaves behind. All regenerable from the source markdown.
# Narration working directories: WAV masters and delivery files, gigabytes per book.
# Deliverables live in the site repo; these are reproducible from markdown and a seed.
/narration/
/narration-*/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Narration run logs from scripts/narrate-*.sh.
*.log
